    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Iijfr",
      "x": 1753,
      "y": 2526,
      "name": "NOTE/System",
      "width": 380,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "ENSEMBLE DESIGN SYSTEM - READ ME FIRST (for any agent building screens)\n\nFeel: Soft. Warm. Confidential. A trusted friend's opinion, never a lab report.\n\nHard rules:\n1. Every fill/text color MUST use a $token - never hardcode hex. Tokens are mode-themed; set theme {mode: dark} on a screen frame to get dark mode free.\n2. Backgrounds are $bg, cards are $surface-card. Pure white/black never appear.\n3. No red/yellow/green severity colors anywhere near skin data.\n4. Nothing sharp: min radius 10, cards 20-28, all pills radius-full.\n5. Newsreader = headlines + emotional lines (rationale). Inter = everything functional.\n6. One primary action per screen, CTA anchored bottom, thumb-reachable, min 44px tall.\n7. Screens are 390 wide, fit_content(844) height, single column, pad-screen 20 left/right.\n8. Petal scatter: only at edges/corners, always cropped by the container, tone-on-tone ($petal-1/2/3), never under text. Toast 1 petal, card 2-3, empty state 4-5.\n9. Loading is never a spinner: use UI/ProgressPetals (the bloom assembling) with staged copy from docs/CONTENT.md section 3.\n10. Copy voice: see docs/CONTENT.md. Banned words: severity, flaw, problem, damage, poor."
    },
