    {
      "id": "n8F9xQ",
      "type": "ref",
      "ref": "b9ls8C",
      "name": "ScreenShell (dark demo)",
      "x": 2109,
      "y": 3513,
      "theme": {
        "mode": "dark"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "OMcX0",
      "x": 1639,
      "y": 4433,
      "name": "NOTE/Components",
      "width": 420,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "COMPONENT USAGE (exact names matter - instance these, never redraw)\n\nUI/ScreenShell - start EVERY app screen as an instance of this. StatusBar on top, ContentSlot for the body, CTAZone pinned at the bottom. Replace ContentSlot children; override CTA label via descendants. For dark mode set theme {mode:dark} on the instance - all tokens flip automatically (see dark demo alongside).\n\nUI/ProgressPetals - THE loading indicator (never use a spinner). It is the bloom with 7 petals named Petal0..Petal6. To show progress stage N, override enabled:false on petals N..6 in the instance. Pair with staged copy: reading your skin / choosing your palette / matching outfit and beauty / putting your look together.\n\nUI/ButtonPrimary - one per screen max, width fill_container inside CTAZone. Label is verb-first and specific: 'Scan your face', 'Get your look' - never 'Continue' alone if a specific verb exists.\n\nUI/Chip + UI/ChipSelected - questionnaire answers, tap-only, stacked or wrapped rows, never free text.\n\nUI/PrivacyBadge - REQUIRED on both capture screens (face + body), sits directly under the capture control.\n\nUI/TrustFooter - REQUIRED on any screen showing skin data or the final Look. Never dismissible.\n\nUI/Card - base surface for content blocks. Add petal scatter to a card by inserting 2-3 petal paths (copy from Brand Experiments > Sec5) at corners, always cropped, fills $petal-1/2/3 only.\n\nLogo/Mark, Logo/Lockup - brand. Mark scales only via descendant overrides (all four children share the same width/height override).\n\nSeason blooms (Brand Experiments Sec2) - use tonal ramps only, one hue family per bloom. NEVER cycle unrelated hues across petals."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "N0rcY",
      "x": 2109,
      "y": 4433,
      "name": "NOTE/ScreenRecipes",
      "width": 420,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "SCREEN RECIPES (the 8 app screens - full spec in docs/DEVELOPMENT.md section 4, copy rules in docs/CONTENT.md)\n\n1 Occasion entry: display type 'Let's get you ready.' + UI/Input (sparkles icon) + country input variant (map-pin) + CTA. No progress bar here - ease in.\n2 Face capture: NavHeader + camera viewport card (radius-xl, 3:4) + lighting guidance line (directional copy, never 'lighting insufficient') + UI/PrivacyBadge + CTA.\n3 Skin snapshot: 'Your skin, at a glance' card pattern (see Brand Experiments Sec5) - strengths first, max 3 focus chips, empowering language only + UI/TrustFooter.\n4 Questionnaire: one question visible at a time, big chips, gap-sm between, progress dots.\n5 Body capture: same as face capture + pose guide overlay (translucent outline) + PrivacyBadge. Highest-anxiety screen - most whitespace.\n6 Composing: full-bleed $bg, UI/ProgressPetals large (120px) centered, staged copy fading below, petal scatter sparse at edges. A waiting room that feels good.\n7 The Look: hero image card (VTO result, radius-xl) > rationale in Newsreader 19 with generous line-height > shoppable rows (quieter than hero) > UI/TrustFooter. Single column, hero is the star.\n8 Share card: 340x200 landscape, see Brand Experiments Sec4 - bloom cropped at corner, palette dots, small lockup.\n\nFlyers/marketing: same tokens, Newsreader display sizes up to 56, petal scatter denser (6-8) allowed, always the picked-cosmos mark, light mode default."
    },
