    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "OHPrs",
      "x": 2073,
      "y": 5651,
      "name": "NOTE/Responsive",
      "width": 420,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "RESPONSIVE STRATEGY (mobile-first, but desktop is what judges open first)\n\nBreakpoints:\n- under 768: mobile layouts exactly as designed (UI/ScreenShell).\n- 768 to 1023 (tablet): same single centered column, width 480-560, margin scatter appears.\n- 1024 and up (desktop): two patterns, never a stretched phone.\n\nPattern 1 - THE STAGE (all flow screens: occasion, capture, questionnaire, composing): the mobile column (480 max) floats centered on the warm $bg canvas inside a radius-xl outlined card. The extra canvas is brand space: petal scatter on the margins (6-8 petals, tone-on-tone, plus 2-3 gold specks), NEVER content. Do not invent desktop-only features for these screens.\n\nPattern 2 - TWO-COLUMN (Look screen, landing page): max-width 1080 centered. Look: hero VTO card 560 left (sticky on scroll), rationale + shoppable rows + TrustFooter right. Landing: per docs/LANDING.md sections, display type up to 56.\n\nRules that never change across breakpoints: tap targets 44px min, one primary CTA, token-only colors, scatter never under text, TrustFooter wherever skin data shows.\n\nCamera capture on desktop: file-upload variant of the capture card (drag-drop plus browse), same PrivacyBadge placement."
    },
