    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Ulpy2",
      "x": -26,
      "y": 7761,
      "name": "NOTE/HeroMasonry",
      "width": 430,
      "height": 1573,
      "content": "HERO MASONRY MARQUEE (the animated image wall)\n\nLAYOUT (desktop): the masonry is FULL-BLEED to the TOP edge of the viewport (and the right edge) - images start at the very tip of the screen and run off top + bottom, no padding above them. The nav (logo + links + CTA) floats OVER the left content column only, never over the images. Hero headline/CTA sit on the left; masonry occupies the right ~40% edge-to-edge.\n\nDESKTOP (vertical motion): 4 images per column, 3 columns of beauty/fashion PRODUCTS (skincare, silk, lipstick, jewelry, eyeshadow, perfume, brushes, fabric, blush, nail polish, cream - NO human faces/models/hands). Columns scroll on a slow infinite loop, ALTERNATING: Col A up, Col B down, Col C up. ~45-60s per cycle, constant linear speed (never stops). Columns start at DIFFERENT vertical offsets so image edges never line up in a row - staggered masonry, and the top row is intentionally cut by the screen tip.\n\nMOBILE (horizontal motion): rotate 90deg - 2-3 horizontal ROWS scrolling sideways, alternating: Row 1 left, Row 2 right. Same stagger + slow loop. Mobile hero is NOT full-bleed-top (nav sits above normally).\n\nSEAMLESS LOOP: duplicate each column/row image set back-to-back, translate by one set length, reset. Rounded images (radius-md), soft shadow, varied heights (masonry).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: honor prefers-reduced-motion - freeze staggered/static. Faint $bg gradient scrim at the top edge keeps the floating nav legible over the images. Transform-only animation (GPU-cheap): CSS keyframes translateY/translateX or motion/Framer."
    }
  ],
